## 5. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)

**Q: What makes CBT-I different from standard sleep hygiene?**
A: Sleep hygiene tips (e.g., cool room, dark curtains, avoiding caffeine) address ambient sleep conditions, but do not alter conditioned neurological arousal or homeostatic sleep debt. Once insomnia becomes chronic, sleep hygiene alone is insufficient because the brain has developed conditioned arousal in response to the bed itself. CBT-I directly addresses this conditioned response through sleep restriction and stimulus control.

**Q: Can CBT-I be conducted alongside psychiatric medication?**
A: Yes. CBT-I is fully compatible with existing medication regimens. When appropriate and desired by the client, Grey Wellness coordinates with the client's prescriber to support a gradual, physician-supervised medication taper once natural sleep architecture is restored.

**Q: Are sessions available in Spanish?**
A: Yes. All clinical assessments, CBT-I sleep logs, homework exercises, and therapy sessions are available in fluent native Spanish (*Terapia Cognitivo Conductual para el Insomnio en Español*).

